        </aside>
      </div>

      <section class="editorial" aria-label="Editorial notes">
        <h2>Reporting and source notes</h2>

        <details open>
          <summary>Before publication: requests for response</summary>
          <div>
            <p>This draft has not been sent externally. Before publication, provide Sagamok Chief and Council, the Political Office, the Director of Finance and GR Truss with the central facts and a reasonable opportunity to respond.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Was the original $500,000 plus 4 per cent repaid? If so, on what date and in what amount?</li>
              <li>Was the repayment deadline extended? If so, who approved the extension and when?</li>
              <li>What balance remains on the original and May 2026 advances?</li>
              <li>What record authorized the three director and officer roles effective April 1, 2025?</li>
              <li>What agreement underlies PPSR file 512630307, and what is its current status?</li>
              <li>Invite correction of any factual error and include the response fairly.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Primary source register</summary>
          <div>
            <ul>
              <li>Sagamok FY2025 audited consolidated financial statements, Note 18.</li>
              <li>Council minutes: April 2, May 27 and September 23, 2025; January 22, April 7, April 18, May 12 and May 19, 2026.</li>
              <li>Certified Ontario Business Registry profile for 2262012 Ontario Limited.</li>
              <li>Certified Ontario PPSR search for 2262012 Ontario Limited, file 512630307.</li>
              <li>Certified OnLand parcel register PIN 31502-0809.</li>
              <li>Each visual was checked against the listed audit, Council, registry, PPSR and land-register records.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Editorial boundary</summary>
          <div>
            <p>The held record establishes the approvals, deadlines, corporate dates and registered overlap. It does not establish non-payment, an improper appointment, an improper security arrangement or wrongdoing. The missing agreements and accounting records decide those questions.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
